            <ArticleTitle>The role of bupivacaine in post-tonsillectomy pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>278-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The peritonsillar tissues on one side of 45 consecutive patients undergoing tonsillectomy were infiltrated with bupivacaine and adrenaline, the opposite side serving as a control. Although a significant difference was noted between the two sides this was not a substantial difference in terms of pain relief.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
